From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CatPieLeaf <catpieleaf@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 20:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amd/display: stop advertising RGBA8888 plane format

amdgpu_dm advertises DRM_FORMAT_RGBA8888 in rgb_formats and
overlay_formats, but fill_dc_plane_info_and_addr() has no case for it
and DC has no RGBA8888 surface format to map it to. A compositor that
picks the advertised format gets its commit rejected:

  amdgpu 0000:03:00.0: [drm] *ERROR* Unsupported screen format RA24 little-endian (0x34324152)
  kwin_wayland: Atomic modeset commit failed! Invalid argument

Seen with KWin on an RX 9070 (Navi 48) under Fedora 7.2.7, at session
start and after resume. Mainline still has the mismatch.

Drop RGBA8888 from both advertised lists, and from the per-pixel alpha
list, which no framebuffer can reach any more. Nothing that works today
is lost: every RGBA8888 framebuffer already failed in
fill_dc_plane_info_and_addr().
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_plane.c | 3 ---
 1 file changed, 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_plane.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_plane.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_plane.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_plane.c
@@ -50,7 +50,6 @@
 static const uint32_t rgb_formats[] = {
 	DRM_FORMAT_XRGB8888,
 	DRM_FORMAT_ARGB8888,
-	DRM_FORMAT_RGBA8888,
 	DRM_FORMAT_XRGB2101010,
 	DRM_FORMAT_XBGR2101010,
 	DRM_FORMAT_ARGB2101010,
@@ -67,7 +66,6 @@
 static const uint32_t overlay_formats[] = {
 	DRM_FORMAT_XRGB8888,
 	DRM_FORMAT_ARGB8888,
-	DRM_FORMAT_RGBA8888,
 	DRM_FORMAT_XBGR8888,
 	DRM_FORMAT_ABGR8888,
 	DRM_FORMAT_RGB565,
@@ -112,7 +110,6 @@
 		plane_state->pixel_blend_mode == DRM_MODE_BLEND_COVERAGE) {
 		static const uint32_t alpha_formats[] = {
 			DRM_FORMAT_ARGB8888,
-			DRM_FORMAT_RGBA8888,
 			DRM_FORMAT_ABGR8888,
 			DRM_FORMAT_ARGB2101010,
 			DRM_FORMAT_ABGR2101010,
